From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RenderingDevice: read a buffer the GPU never writes without
 waiting

buffer_get_data() copies a buffer on the GPU and then waits for the GPU
to finish every frame in flight, a stall of a frame or two: in VR at
72 Hz, 24 to 33 ms for Mesh.surface_get_arrays() on a mesh just loaded.

A buffer made with its data, on a device that can map it (any with
unified memory, Apple Silicon's among them), is written by the CPU when
it's made. Anything that writes a buffer on the GPU's timeline (an
update, a copy, a clear, a shader writing it) gives it a draw tracker
first, so one with none still holds what it was made with: its data is
now read straight from it. Meshes' vertex and index buffers are such
buffers, unless they're skinned, have blend shapes or are updated.

No upstream issue yet.

Test: a vertex buffer made with its data reads back what it was made
with, and after an update, the update (Purr's samples/graphics, in a
window).
---
 godot/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/godot/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp b/godot/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp
index 6f266f14..0c0b83a8 100644
--- a/godot/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp
+++ b/godot/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp
@@ -1369,6 +1369,19 @@ Vector<uint8_t> RenderingDevice::buffer_get_data(RID p_buffer, uint32_t p_offset
 				"Size is larger than the buffer.");
 	}
 
+	if (buffer->alloc_type == RDD::MEMORY_ALLOCATION_TYPE_GPU_MAPPABLE && buffer->draw_tracker == nullptr) {
+		// The CPU wrote this buffer when it was made, and nothing has written it since: anything
+		// written on the GPU's timeline (an update, a copy, a shader) gives it a tracker first.
+		// Read straight from it, rather than waiting for the GPU to finish every frame in flight.
+		const uint8_t *buffer_mem = driver->buffer_map(buffer->driver_id);
+		ERR_FAIL_NULL_V(buffer_mem, Vector<uint8_t>());
+		Vector<uint8_t> buffer_data;
+		buffer_data.resize(p_size);
+		memcpy(buffer_data.ptrw(), buffer_mem + p_offset, p_size);
+		driver->buffer_unmap(buffer->driver_id);
+		return buffer_data;
+	}
+
 	_check_transfer_worker_buffer(buffer);
 
 	RDD::BufferID tmp_buffer = driver->buffer_create(buffer->size, RDD::BUFFER_USAGE_TRANSFER_TO_BIT, RDD::MEMORY_ALLOCATION_TYPE_CPU, frames_drawn);
